[E4428c1] {"title":"Qaumi Taranah","text":"Qaumi Taranah
rɑː. nɑ ) , lit . `` National Anthem '' ) , also known as Pāk Sarzamīn ( Urdu : پاک سرزمین ‬ ‎ , pronounced ( ˈpɑːk ˈsər. zə. miːn ) , lit . `` The Sacred Land '' ) , is the national anthem of Pakistan . Its music was composed by Ahmad G. Chagla in 1949 , preceding the lyrics , which were written by Hafeez Jullundhri in 1952 . It was officially adopted as Pakistan 's national anthem in August 1954 and was recorded in the same year by eleven major singers of Pakistan including Ahmad Rushdi , Kaukab Jahan , Rasheeda Begum , Najam Ara , Naseema Shaheen , Zawar Hussain , Akhtar Abbas , Ghulam Dastagir , Anwar Zaheer and Akhtar Wasi Ali .","entities":["Hafeez Jullundhri","Kaukab Jahan","Rasheeda Begum","Najam Ara","Naseema Shaheen","Zawar Hussain","Akhtar Abbas","Ghulam Dastagir","Anwar Zaheer","Akhtar Wasi Ali","Composition of the music","Writing of the lyrics","Official adoption as Pakistan's national anthem","Recording of Qaumi Taranah","Ahmad G. Chagla"],"facts":["Hafeez Jullundhri -MEMBER_OF-> National Anthem Committee","Hafeez Jullundhri -PARTICIPATED_IN-> First public broadcast of Qaumi Taranah","Hafeez Jullundhri -CREATED-> Urdu lyrics","Hafeez Jullundhri -RELATED_TO-> Selection of verses","Kaukab Jahan -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Performance of Qaumi Taranah"]}
