[E109a14] {"title":"Qaumi Taranah","text":"Qaumi Taranah
In 1950 , the impending state visit of the Shah of Iran added urgency to the matter and resulted in the Government of Pakistan asking the NAC to submit an anthem without further delay . The NAC Chairman , then Federal Minister for Education , Fazlur Rahman , asked several poets and composers to write lyrics but none of the submitted works were deemed suitable . The NAC also examined several different tunes and eventually selected the one presented by Ahmed G. Chagla and submitted it for formal approval . On 21 August 1949 , the Government of Pakistan adopted Chagla 's tune for the national anthem . The anthem , without lyrics , was performed for the first time for a foreign head of state on the state visit of the Shah of Iran to Pakistan in Karachi on 1 March 1950 by a Pakistan Navy band . It was later played for Prime Minister Liaquat Ali Khan during his official visit to the United States on 3 May 1950 . It was played before the NAC on 10 August 1950 . Official recognition to the national anthem , however , was not given until August 1954 .","entities":["Shah of Iran","United States","Government of Pakistan","NAC","Ahmed G. Chagla","Fazlur Rahman","Pakistan Navy band","State visit of the Shah of Iran to Pakistan","Liaquat Ali Khan","Official visit of Liaquat Ali Khan to the United States","Adoption of the tune for the national anthem","Playing of the anthem before the NAC","Official recognition of the national anthem","Qaumi Taranah","Pakistan"],"facts":["Shah of Iran -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Shah of Iran's use of the Cyrus Cylinder as a central image","United States -PART_OF-> Beekeeping by countries","United States -PART_OF-> Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Northern America","United States -PART_OF-> these ten countries"]}
