Worldwide , this is one of the largest use for lithium compounds . Glazes containing lithium oxides are used for ovenware . Lithium carbonate ( Li CO ) is generally used in this application because it converts to the oxide upon heating . Electrical and electronics ( edit ) Late in the 20th century , lithium became an important component of battery electrolytes and electrodes , because of its high electrode potential . Because of its low atomic mass , it has a high charge - and power - to - weight ratio . A typical lithium - ion battery can generate approximately 3 volts per cell , compared with 2.1 volts for lead - acid or 1.5 volts for zinc - carbon cells . Lithium - ion batteries , which are rechargeable and have a high energy density , should not be confused with lithium batteries , which are disposable ( primary ) batteries with lithium or its compounds as the anode . Other rechargeable batteries that use lithium include the lithium - ion polymer battery , lithium iron phosphate battery , and the nanowire battery . Lubricating greases ( edit ) Main article : Lithium grease The third most common use of lithium is in greases .","entities":["glazes","lithium oxides","ovenware","electrical and electronics","battery electrolytes","electrodes","lithium-ion battery","lead-acid cells","zinc-carbon cells","lithium-ion polymer battery","nanowire battery","greases","lithium grease","Lithium carbonate","lithium batteries"],"facts":["IPU -RELATED_TO-> lithium-ion battery","Electric car -RELATED_TO-> lithium-ion battery","lithium oxide -RELATED_TO-> glazes","glazes -RELATED_TO-> thermal expansion","Lithium carbonate -RELATED_TO-> Continuous casting mould flux slags"]}
