[Ebacdb7] {"title":"The Great Gatsby","text":"The Great Gatsby
Considered to be Fitzgerald 's magnum opus , The Great Gatsby explores themes of decadence , idealism , resistance to change , social upheaval , and excess , creating a portrait of the Jazz Age or the Roaring Twenties that has been described as a cautionary tale regarding the American Dream . Fitzgerald -- inspired by the parties he had attended while visiting Long Island 's north shore -- began planning the novel in 1923 , desiring to produce , in his words , `` something new -- something extraordinary and beautiful and simple and intricately patterned . '' Progress was slow , with Fitzgerald completing his first draft following a move to the French Riviera in 1924 . His editor , Maxwell Perkins , felt the book was vague and persuaded the author to revise over the following winter . Fitzgerald was repeatedly ambivalent about the book 's title and he considered a variety of alternatives , including titles that referenced the Roman character Trimalchio ; the title he was last documented to have desired was Under the Red , White , and Blue .","entities":["French Riviera","decadence","idealism","resistance to change","social upheaval","excess","planning The Great Gatsby","move to the French Riviera","completion of the first draft of The Great Gatsby","Fitzgerald","Trimalchio","The Great Gatsby","Jazz Age","American Dream","Maxwell Perkins"],"facts":["Fitzgerald -LOCATED_IN-> Capri","Fitzgerald -LOCATED_IN-> Rome","Fitzgerald -LOCATED_IN-> Camp Sheridan","Fitzgerald -LOCATED_IN-> Great Neck","Fitzgerald -RELATED_TO-> Long Island's north shore"]}

