energy diagram The reaction mechanism , involving the heterogeneous catalyst , is believed to involve the following steps : N ( g ) → N ( adsorbed ) N ( adsorbed ) → 2 N ( adsorbed ) H ( g ) → H ( adsorbed ) H ( adsorbed ) → 2 H ( adsorbed ) N ( adsorbed ) + 3 H ( adsorbed ) → NH ( adsorbed ) NH ( adsorbed ) → NH ( g ) Reaction 5 occurs in three steps , forming NH , NH , and then NH . Experimental evidence points to reaction 2 as being the slow , rate - determining step . This is not unexpected since the bond broken , the nitrogen triple bond , is the strongest of the bonds that must be broken . A major contributor to the elucidation of this mechanism is Gerhard Ertl . Economic and environmental aspects ( edit ) Further information : Ammonia production § Sustainable ammonia production Industrial fertilizer plant When it was first invented , the Haber process needed to compete against another industrial process , the Cyanamide process .","entities":["Haber process","reaction mechanism","heterogeneous catalyst","reaction 2","reaction 5","nitrogen triple bond","Gerhard Ertl","Ammonia production","Sustainable ammonia production","Cyanamide process"],"facts":["Haber process -RELATED_TO-> demonstration of the Haber process","Haber process -RELATED_TO-> industrial-scale ammonia manufacture","Haber process -RELATED_TO-> German war effort","Haber process -RELATED_TO-> German war effort","Haber process -RELATED_TO-> ammonia"]}
