In February 1952 , on her accession , Elizabeth II was proclaimed as sovereign separately throughout her realms . In October 2011 , the heads of government of all 16 realms agreed unanimously at a meeting held in Perth , Australia , to proposed changes to the royal succession laws that would see the order of succession for people born after 28 October 2011 governed by absolute primogeniture -- wherein succession passes to an individual 's children according to birth order , regardless of gender -- instead of male - preference primogeniture . They also agreed to lift a ban on those who marry Roman Catholics . The ban on Catholics themselves was retained to ensure that the monarch would be in communion with the Church of England . The changes came into effect across the Commonwealth realms on 26 March 2015 , after legislation was made according to each realm 's constitution . Following the changes coming into effect , the positions of the first 27 in line remained unchanged , including Princess Anne and her children and grandchildren , until the birth of Princess Charlotte of Cambridge on 2 May 2015 .","entities":["Australia","Commonwealth realms","absolute primogeniture","male-preference primogeniture","Roman Catholics","Princess Anne","Elizabeth II","Accession of Elizabeth II","Meeting of heads of government of all 16 realms","Heads of government of all 16 realms","Perth","Proposal of changes to the royal succession laws","Royal succession laws","Changes to royal succession laws came into effect","Princess Charlotte of Cambridge"],"facts":["Australia -PART_OF-> Cairns Group","Australia -PART_OF-> British Empire","Australia -PART_OF-> Northern Territory","Australia -PART_OF-> Tasmania","Australia -PART_OF-> Jervis Bay Territory"]}
