As stipulated at the Jimaguayü Assembly two years earlier , a second Constituent Assembly met in La Yaya , Camagüey , on October 10 , 1897 . The newly adopted constitution provided that military command was to be subordinated to civilian rule . The government was confirmed , naming Bartolomé Masó President and Domingo Méndez Capote Vice President . Madrid decided to change its policy towards Cuba , and replaced Weyler . It also drew up a colonial constitution for Cuba and Puerto Rico , and installed a new government in Havana . But with half the country out of its control and the other half in arms , the colonial government was powerless and these changes were rejected by the rebels . The Maine incident Main article : USS Maine ( ACR - 1 ) Wreckage of the Maine , 1898 The Cuban struggle for independence had captured the American imagination for years . Some newspapers had agitated for US intervention , especially because of its large financial investment , and featured sensational stories of Spanish atrocities against the native Cuban population , which were exaggerated for propaganda . Such coverage continued after Spain had replaced Weyler and changed its policies .","entities":["Cuban War of Independence","Bartolomé Masó","rebels","Jimaguayü Assembly","second Constituent Assembly","Meeting of the second Constituent Assembly","La Yaya","Domingo Méndez Capote","Weyler","colonial constitution for Cuba and Puerto Rico","Maine incident","USS Maine (ACR - 1)","US intervention","newspapers","colonial government"],"facts":["Cuban War of Independence -RELATED_TO-> Philippines","Cuban War of Independence -LOCATED_IN-> Pinar del Rio","Cuban War of Independence -LOCATED_IN-> Matanzas","Cuban War of Independence -LOCATED_IN-> Oriente","Cuban War of Independence -RELATED_TO-> Florida"]}

