Ossification center - wikipedia Ossification center Jump to : navigation , search This article needs additional citations for verification . Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources . Unsourced material may be challenged and removed . ( May 2011 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this template message ) Ossification center X-ray of ossification centers in a child . Details Identifiers Latin centrum ossificationis Dorlands / Elsevier 12227335 TA A02. 0.00. 043 FMA 75436 Anatomical terminology ( edit on Wikidata ) The first step in ossification of the cartilage is that the cartilage cells , at the point where ossification is commencing and which is termed as an ossification center , enlarge and arrange themselves in rows . The matrix in which they are imbedded increases in quantity , so that the cells become further separated from each other . A deposit of calcareous material now takes place in this matrix , between the rows of cells , so that they become separated from each other by longitudinal columns of calcified matrix , presenting a granular and opaque appearance .","entities":["cartilage cells","matrix","calcareous material","calcified matrix","Ossification center","Ossification","Cartilage"],"facts":["Ossification center -RELATED_TO-> Limb development","Ossification center -RELATED_TO-> Limb bud","Ossification center -RELATED_TO-> Development of bone","Ossification center -RELATED_TO-> Triradiate cartilage","Ossification center -RELATED_TO-> Apical ectodermal ridge"]}
