This led to the discovery that the twins had different fathers . In 1982 , twins who were born with two different skin colors were discovered to be conceived as a result of heteropaternal superfecundation . In 2001 , a case of spontaneous monopaternal superfecundation was reported after a woman undergoing IVF treatments gave birth to quintuplets after only two embryos were implanted . Genetic testing supported that the twinning was not a result of the embryos splitting , and that all five boys shared the same father . In 2016 , an IVF - implanted surrogate mother gave birth to two children : one genetically unrelated child from an implanted embryo , and a biological child from her own egg and her husband 's sperm . See also ( edit ) Castor and Pollux , said to be twins having different fathers Chimera ( genetics ) Mixed twins Polyspermy References ( edit ) Jump up ^ Worland , Justin ( May 8 , 2015 ) . `` The Science of How Women Can Have Twins With 2 Different Fathers '' . Time . Retrieved March 23 , 2017 .","entities":["Polyspermy","Heteropaternal superfecundation","Spontaneous monopaternal superfecundation","IVF","Discovery of twins born with two different skin colors","Reported case of spontaneous monopaternal superfecundation","Birth of two children to an IVF-implanted surrogate mother","Genetic testing","Twinning","Justin Worland","The Science of How Women Can Have Twins With 2 Different Fathers","Castor and Pollux","Chimera (genetics)","Mixed twins","Superfecundation"],"facts":["Polyspermy -RELATED_TO-> sperm","Polyspermy -RELATED_TO-> egg","Heteropaternal superfecundation -RELATED_TO-> Mammals","Heteropaternal superfecundation -RELATED_TO-> fertilization","Heteropaternal superfecundation -RELATED_TO-> humans"]}
