He did songwriting wherever he could , including on buses , and used an upright piano above the Birdland Club in New York City . One of the causes of this early nomadic life as a songwriter was due to his songs having too many words : `` I 'd spent a lot of time on lyrics , and they were looking for hooks , and I did n't really understand the nature of that , '' he says . During those lean years , he was only able to sell about one song a week , barely enough to survive on . He found himself only earning enough to spend 35 cents a day on food ( US $3 in 2017 dollars ) . However , the privacy he had above the Birdland Club allowed him to focus on writing without distractions ; as he explained , `` Something new began to happen . I was n't under the gun , and suddenly interesting songs began to happen , songs that had things none of the others did . '' Among them were `` Cherry , Cherry '' and `` Solitary Man '' . `` Solitary Man '' was the first record that Diamond recorded in his own name that made the charts .","entities":["New York City","Birdland Club","Cherry, Cherry","upright piano","Solitary Man","Neil Diamond"],"facts":["New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New Jersey","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New York","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New York (state)","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> North America","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> United States"]}
[Eec9d9e] {"title":"The Rolling Stones","text":"The Rolling Stones
Later in 1963 Oldham and Easton arranged the band 's first big UK concert tour as a supporting act for American stars including Bo Diddley , Little Richard and the Everly Brothers . The tour gave the band the opportunity to hone their stagecraft . During the tour the band recorded their second single , a Lennon -- McCartney - penned number entitled `` I Wanna Be Your Man '' ; it reached No. 12 in the UK charts . `` I Wanna Be Your Man '' was written and given to the Stones when John Lennon and Paul McCartney visited them in the studio as the two Beatles liked to give the copyrights to songs away to their friends . A Beatles version of the song was also recorded and released on the 1963 album With the Beatles . The third single by the Stones , Buddy Holly 's `` Not Fade Away '' , itself based on Bo Diddley 's style , was released in February 1964 and reached No. 3 . Oldham saw little future for an act that lost significant songwriting royalties by playing songs of what he described as `` middle - aged blacks '' , limiting the appeal to teenage audiences .","entities":["John Lennon","Little Richard","The Beatles","Paul McCartney","Oldham","Easton","The band's first big UK concert tour","Bo Diddley","The Everly Brothers","I Wanna Be Your Man","With the Beatles","Bo Diddley's style","The Rolling Stones","Buddy Holly","UK"],"facts":["John Lennon -RELATED_TO-> Monday Night Football","John Lennon -RELATED_TO-> Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band","John Lennon -RELATED_TO-> A Day in the Life","John Lennon -RELATED_TO-> Where Have You Been (All My Life)","John Lennon -RELATED_TO-> A Whiter Shade of Pale"]}

