[E34f49d] {"title":"Church Fathers","text":"Church Fathers
Christian Fathers , or Fathers of the Church are ancient and generally influential Christian theologians , some of whom were eminent teachers and great bishops . The term is used of writers or teachers of the Church not necessarily ordained and not necessarily `` saints '' -- Origen Adamantius and Tertullian are often considered Church Fathers , but are not saints , owing to their views later being deemed heretical . Most Church Fathers are honored as saints in the Catholic Church , the Eastern Orthodox Church , Oriental Orthodoxy , the Church of the East , Anglicanism and Lutheranism , as well as other churches and groups . The era of these scholars who set the theological and scholarly foundations of Christianity largely ended by 700 AD . While western churches regard only early teachers of Christianity as Fathers , the Orthodox Church honors as `` Fathers '' many saints far beyond the early centuries of church history , even to the present day . Contents ( hide ) 1 Great Fathers 2 Apostolic Fathers 2.1 Clement of Rome 2.2 Ignatius of Antioch 2.3 Polycarp of Smyrna 2.4 Papias of Hierapolis 3 Greek Fathers 3.1 Justin Martyr 3.","entities":["Christianity","Origen Adamantius","Oriental Orthodoxy","Church of the East","Anglicanism","Lutheranism","Western churches","Greek Fathers","Apostolic Fathers","Clement of Rome","Ignatius of Antioch","Polycarp of Smyrna","Papias of Hierapolis","Justin Martyr","Tertullian"],"facts":["Christianity -RELATED_TO-> Hawaii","Christianity -RELATED_TO-> Australia","Christianity -RELATED_TO-> nature","Christianity -RELATED_TO-> Christian chivalry","Christianity -RELATED_TO-> Mormons"]}
