Patristics ( edit ) Main article : Patristics The study of the Church Fathers is known as `` Patristics '' . Works of fathers in early Christianity , prior to Nicene Christianity , were translated into English in a 19th - century collection Ante - Nicene Fathers . Those of the First Council of Nicaea and continuing through the Second Council of Nicea ( 787 ) are collected in Nicene and Post-Nicene Fathers . See also ( edit ) Confessor of the Faith Doctor of the Church Great Church Historiography of early Christianity List of Church Fathers List of Eastern Orthodox saint titles Patron Saints of Europe Sacred tradition References ( edit ) ^ Jump up to : Herbermann , Charles , ed. ( 1913 ) . `` Fathers of the Church '' . Catholic Encyclopedia . New York : Robert Appleton Company .","entities":["New York","English","First Council of Nicaea","Doctor of the Church","sacred tradition","Patristics","early Christianity","Nicene Christianity","Ante-Nicene Fathers","Second Council of Nicea","Nicene and Post-Nicene Fathers","Confessor of the Faith","Great Church","Historiography of early Christianity","List of Church Fathers"],"facts":["New York -PART_OF-> US","Rochester -PART_OF-> New York","Brooklyn -PART_OF-> New York","Mount Pleasant -PART_OF-> New York","New York -PART_OF-> United States"]}
