In Chile , the highway follows Chile Route 5 south to a point north of Santiago ( Llaillay ) , where the highway splits into two parts , one of which goes through Chilean territory to Puerto Montt , where it splits again , to Quellón on Chiloé Island , and to its continuation as the Carretera Austral . The other part goes east along Chile Route 60 , which becomes Argentina National Route 7 at the Argentinian border and continues to Buenos Aires , the end of the main highway . The highway network also continues south of Buenos Aires along Argentina National Route 3 towards the city of Ushuaia in Tierra del Fuego . Another branch , from Buenos Aires to Asunción in Paraguay , heads out of Buenos Aires on Argentina National Route 9 . It switches to Argentina National Route 11 at Rosario , which crosses the border with Paraguay right at Asunción . Other branches probably exist across the center of South America .","entities":["Paraguay","Argentina","Tierra del Fuego","South America","Chile","Santiago","Pan-American Highway","Puerto Montt","Quellón","Ushuaia","Chile Route 5","Llaillay","Chiloé Island","Carretera Austral","Chile Route 60"],"facts":["Paraguay -LOCATED_IN-> Americas","Zara -LOCATED_IN-> Paraguay","Alto Paraná -LOCATED_IN-> Paraguay","Ñandutí, 1020 AM -LOCATED_IN-> Paraguay","Paraguay -RELATED_TO-> Paraguayan embassy"]}
