[E5fff5d] {"title":"Geography of Nigeria","text":"Geography of Nigeria
Plains rise to the north of the valleys . To the southwest of the Niger there is `` rugged '' highland , and to the southeast of the Benue hills and mountains are found all the way to the border with Cameroon . Coastal plains are found in both the southwest and the southeast . Niger Delta ( edit ) This section needs expansion . You can help by adding to it . ( January 2011 ) The Niger Delta is located in the southern part of Nigeria . It is one of the world 's largest arcuate fan - shaped river deltas . The riverine area of the Niger Delta is a coastal belt of swamps bordering the Atlantic ocean . The swamps are vegetated tidal flats formed by a reticulate pattern of interconnected meandering creeks and distributaries of the River Niger . Vegetation of the Niger Delta ( edit ) The vegetation of the Niger Delta consist mainly of forest swamps . The forest are of two types , nearest the sea is a belt of saline / brackish Mangrove swamp separated from the sea by sand beach ridges within the mangrove swamp . Numerous sandy islands occur with fresh water vegetation .","entities":["River Niger","coastal plains","valleys","highland","hills and mountains","coastal belt of swamps","creeks","distributaries","forest swamps","Mangrove swamp","sea","sand beach ridges","sandy islands","fresh water vegetation","riverine area"],"facts":["Pearl oyster -RELATED_TO-> sea","bucket -RELATED_TO-> sea","seal -LOCATED_IN-> sea","turtles hatching -LOCATED_IN-> sea","Niger Delta -LOCATED_IN-> Africa"]}
