citizen ; be at least 35 years old ; be a resident in the U.S. for at least 14 years . A person who meets the above qualifications is still disqualified from holding the office of vice president under the following conditions : Under Article I , Section 3 , Clause 7 , upon conviction in impeachment cases , the Senate has the option of disqualifying convicted individuals from holding federal office , including that of vice president ; Under Section 3 of the Fourteenth Amendment , no person who has swore an oath to support the Constitution , who has later has gone to war against the United States , or given aid and comfort to the nation 's enemies can serve in a state or federal office -- including as vice president . This disqualification , originally aimed at former supporters of the Confederacy , may be removed by a two - thirds vote of each house of the Congress . An additional disqualifying condition may exist under the Twenty - second Amendment , which limits the number of times as person may be elected president to no more than twice .","entities":["United States","Twenty-second Amendment","federal office","Congress","Senate","president","Article I, Section 3, Clause 7","impeachment cases","Section 3 of the Fourteenth Amendment","war against the United States","the nation's enemies","state office","two-thirds vote","each house of the Congress","disqualification"],"facts":["United States -PART_OF-> Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Northern America","United States -PART_OF-> these ten countries","United States -PART_OF-> The Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Beekeeping by countries"]}
