List of World war I battles - wikipedia List of World war I battles Jump to : navigation , search It has been suggested that this article be merged into List of military engagements of World War I. ( Discuss ) Proposed since May 2016 . List of Canadian battles during the First World War on the Western Front plaque in Currie Hall , Royal Military College of Canada Notre - Dame - de-Lorette National Cemetery at Ablain - Saint - Nazaire - the largest single military cemetery in France , holding an ossuary and burials of 40,051 soldiers . Tyne Cot Cemetery at Ypres Salient , Belgium - the largest British military cemetery in the world with more than 35,000 soldiers . World War I , which lasted from July 1914 to November 1918 was , at the time , the largest single war ever to have occurred . There were a large number of allies on each side of the conflict , and their geographical location and that of their imperial provinces meant that parts of the war were fought all over Europe , and in other places such as North Africa , the Middle East , and even minor skirmishes in the Pacific Ocean .","entities":["North Africa","Middle East","Belgium","France","Pacific Ocean","List of military engagements of World War I","List of Canadian battles during the First World War on the Western Front","Currie Hall","Royal Military College of Canada","Notre-Dame-de-Lorette National Cemetery","Ablain-Saint-Nazaire","Tyne Cot Cemetery","Ypres Salient","List of World War I battles","World War I"],"facts":["Libya -LOCATED_IN-> North Africa","Sahara Desert -LOCATED_IN-> North Africa","Afroasiatic -LOCATED_IN-> North Africa","Berber -LOCATED_IN-> North Africa","Deployment to North Africa -LOCATED_IN-> North Africa"]}

[E208c63] {"title":"Toyota","text":"Toyota
However , when Toyota eventually entered the American market in 1957 with the Crown , the name was not well received due to connotations of toys and pets . The name was soon dropped for the American market , but continued in other markets until the mid-1960s . 1960s -- 1970s ( edit ) By the early 1960s , the US had begun placing stiff import tariffs on certain vehicles . The so - called `` chicken tax '' of 1964 placed a 25 % tax on imported light trucks . In response to the tariff , Toyota , Nissan Motor Co. and Honda Motor Co. began building plants in the US by the early 1980s . 1980s ( edit ) With over 40 million sold , the Corolla is one of the most popular and best selling cars in the world . Toyota received its first Japanese Quality Control Award at the start of the 1980s and began participating in a wide variety of motorsports . Due to the 1973 oil crisis , consumers in the lucrative US market began turning to small cars with better fuel economy .","entities":["US","1973 oil crisis","Honda Motor Co.","chicken tax","Nissan Motor Co.","Japanese Quality Control Award","motorsports","Corolla","Crown","Toyota"],"facts":["Washington DC -LOCATED_IN-> US","Missouri -LOCATED_IN-> US","Pennsylvania -LOCATED_IN-> US","US speed limit decrease -LOCATED_IN-> US","US -LOCATED_IN-> Edison Tech Center"]}
