Bāl Kāṇḍ ( edit ) The Child Episode Tulsidas begins the story with an invocation to various deities , his guru , and saints who have preceded him and those who will succeed him in the future . Homage is paid to Valmiki for bringing the Ramayana to the devotees of Rama . Next are introduced and praised the various characters of the epic beginning with the birthplace of Rama , the holy city of Ayodhya . Praises are bestowed on Dasharatha , the king of Ayodhya and Rama 's father , and his queens Kausalya , Kaikeyi and Sumitra . Tulsidas then praises King Janaka , the father - in - law of Rama ) , and his family . He goes on to praise the brothers of Rama - Bharata , Lakshman & Shatrughna and sings the glories of Hanuman , the constant companion to Rama , Sugriva , the monkey king and Jambavan , the leader of bears . Next , the characters of Sita and Rama are introduced . The birth of the four sons of Dasharatha .","entities":["Tulsidas","Ramayana","Bāl Kāṇḍ","Dasharatha","Janaka","Sumitra","Kaikeyi","Rama","Valmiki","Shatrughna","Bharata","Sita","Lakshman","Sugriva","Jambavan"],"facts":["Tulsidas -RELATED_TO-> William Shakespeare","Tulsidas -RELATED_TO-> Vedas","Tulsidas -RELATED_TO-> Puranas","Tulsidas -RELATED_TO-> Upanishads","Tulsidas -RELATED_TO-> Sanskrit"]}
