These extremely arid areas often receive no rain for years . To the north , the Sahara skirts the Mediterranean Sea in Egypt and portions of Libya , but in Cyrenaica and the Maghreb , the Sahara borders the Mediterranean forest , woodland , and scrub eco-regions of northern Africa , all of which have a Mediterranean climate characterized by hot summers and cool and rainy winters . According to the botanical criteria of Frank White and geographer Robert Capot - Rey , the northern limit of the Sahara corresponds to the northern limit of date palm cultivation and the southern limit of the range of esparto , a grass typical of the Mediterranean climate portion of the Maghreb and Iberia . The northern limit also corresponds to the 100 mm ( 3.9 in ) isohyet of annual precipitation . To the south , the Sahara is bounded by the Sahel , a belt of dry tropical savanna with a summer rainy season that extends across Africa from east to west .","entities":["Libya","Cyrenaica","Sahel","Northern Africa","Iberia","Sahara","Maghreb","Mediterranean forest, woodland, and scrub eco-regions","Mediterranean climate","Frank White","Robert Capot-Rey","botanical criteria","date palm cultivation","esparto","100 mm isohyet of annual precipitation"],"facts":["Libya -LOCATED_IN-> North Africa","Libya -LOCATED_IN-> North","2011 civil war -LOCATED_IN-> Libya","Eastern Libya -LOCATED_IN-> Libya","bombing of Libya -LOCATED_IN-> Libya"]}

