Critical reaction to Closing Time was positive . The album 's only single , `` Ol ' ' 55 '' , attracted attention due to a cover version by Waits 's more popular label mates , the Eagles . Other songs from the album were covered by Tim Buckley and Bette Midler . The album was certified Gold in the UK and has gained a contemporary cult following among rock fans . Since its release , the album has been reissued on LP in 1976 , on CD in 1992 and 1999 , and 180 gram LP in 2010 . Contents ( hide ) 1 Background 2 Recording 3 Composition 4 Packaging 5 Release 6 Reception 7 Influence 8 Track listing 9 Personnel 9.1 Musicians 9.2 Guest musicians 9.3 Technical personnel 10 Chart positions 11 Certifications 11.1 References 11.2 Bibliography Background ( edit ) The Troubadour was the site of many early Waits performances Tom Waits began his musical career in 1970 , performing every Monday night at The Troubadour , a venue in Los Angeles , California .","entities":["Los Angeles","rock","Eagles","The Troubadour","Ol' 55","Tim Buckley","Tom Waits","Closing Time","Bette Midler","California","UK"],"facts":["Los Angeles -LOCATED_IN-> United States","Los Angeles -LOCATED_IN-> Mexican Alta California","Los Angeles -LOCATED_IN-> US","Los Angeles -LOCATED_IN-> Calif.","Los Angeles -LOCATED_IN-> Sunset Strip"]}
