She transferred to New Lincoln High School in New York City . As depicted in the 1981 made - for - TV docudrama Crisis at Central High , and as mentioned by Melba Pattillo Beals in Warriors Do n't Cry , white students were punished only when their offense was `` both egregious and witnessed by an adult '' . The drama was based on a book by Elizabeth Huckaby , a vice-principal during the crisis . `` The Lost Year '' In the summer of 1958 , as the school year was drawing to a close , Faubus decided to petition the decision by the Federal District Court in order to postpone the desegregation of public high schools in Little Rock . In the Cooper v. Aaron case , the Little Rock School District , under the leadership of Orval Faubus , fought for a two and a half year delay on de-segregation , which would have meant that black students would only be permitted into public high schools in January 1961 . Faubus argued that if the schools remained integrated there would be an increase in violence .","entities":["New York City","Little Rock Nine","Cooper v. Aaron","Melba Pattillo Beals","Orval Faubus","Warriors Don't Cry","New Lincoln High School","Elizabeth Huckaby","Federal District Court","Little Rock School District","Little Rock","desegregation","Crisis at Central High","Violence"],"facts":["New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New Jersey","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New York","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New York (state)","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> North America","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> United States"]}
