[Ec2e936] {"title":"Lion's mane jellyfish","text":"Lion's mane jellyfish
Two distinct taxa , however , occur together in at least the eastern North Atlantic , with the blue jellyfish ( Cyanea lamarckii Péron & Lesueur , 1810 ) differing in color ( blue , not red ) and smaller size ( 10 -- 20 cm diameter , rarely 35 cm ) . Populations in the western Pacific around Japan are sometimes distinguished as Cyanea nozakii , or as a subspecies , C. c. nozakii . In 2015 , Russian researchers announced a possible sister species , Cyanea tzetlinii found in the White Sea , but this has not yet been recognized by other authoritative databases such as WoRMS or ITIS . Description ( edit ) Lion 's mane jellyfish ( Cyanea capillata ) are named for their showy , trailing tentacles reminiscent of a lion 's mane . They can vary greatly in size : although capable of attaining a bell diameter of over 2 metres ( 6 ft 7 in ) , those found in lower latitudes are much smaller than their far northern counterparts , with a bell about 50 centimetres ( 20 in ) in diameter .","entities":["western Pacific","Japan","blue jellyfish","Cyanea nozakii","Cyanea tzetlinii","eastern North Atlantic","White Sea","WoRMS","ITIS","lion's mane jellyfish"],"facts":["western Pacific populations -LOCATED_IN-> western Pacific","Influence of coral symbionts on feeding preferences of crown-of-thorns starfish Acanthaster planci in the western Pacific -RELATED_TO-> western Pacific","Japan -LOCATED_IN-> Mitsubishi Jeeps","Japan -LOCATED_IN-> Asia","Tokugawa shogunate -LOCATED_IN-> Japan"]}
[E216ff8] {"title":"Lion's mane jellyfish","text":"Lion's mane jellyfish
Lion 's mane jellyfish - wikipedia Lion 's mane jellyfish Jump to : navigation , search Lion 's mane jellyfish Scientific classification Kingdom : Animalia Phylum : Cnidaria Class : Scyphozoa Order : Semaeostomeae Family : Cyaneidae Genus : Cyanea Species : C. capillata Binomial name Cyanea capillata ( Linnaeus , 1758 ) The lion 's mane jellyfish ( Cyanea capillata ) , also known as the giant jellyfish or the hair jelly , is the largest known species of jellyfish . Its range is confined to cold , boreal waters of the Arctic , northern Atlantic , and northern Pacific Oceans . It is common in the English Channel , Irish Sea , North Sea and in western Scandinavian waters south to Kattegat and Øresund . It may also drift in to the south - western part of the Baltic Sea ( where it can not breed due to the low salinity ) . Similar jellyfish -- which may be the same species -- are known to inhabit seas near Australia and New Zealand .","entities":["New Zealand","Australia","Baltic Sea","North Sea","Arctic","northern Atlantic Ocean","northern Pacific Ocean","Irish Sea","western Scandinavian waters","Kattegat","Øresund","lion's mane jellyfish","English Channel"],"facts":["New Zealand -LOCATED_IN-> Oceania","two-way contacts between California and New Zealand -LOCATED_IN-> New Zealand","90-minute two-way contact between New Zealand and England -LOCATED_IN-> New Zealand","Discovery of islands -LOCATED_IN-> New Zealand","New Zealand -LOCATED_IN-> Southwest Pacific"]}
