Informally dubbed as the `` Zaza Pachulia rule '' . Also , officials can now assess if a player is in a shooting motion when determining if a perimeter foul is a shooting or a common foul . The type of foul will be determined on the sequencing of the player 's movement if the foul happens before or after the player starts a shooting motion . Additionally , they can also assess an offensive foul if an offensive player intentionally lunges into the defender or locks arms to create contact , a rule informally dubbed as the `` Harden rule '' . On September 28 , 2017 , the NBA board of governors approved the changes to the draft lottery system to discourage teams from losing on purpose . Starting with the 2018 -- 19 NBA season , the teams with the three worst records will have equal odds at the # 1 pick . In addition , the revised draft lottery will consist of selecting the top four teams instead of the usual three that occurred for over two decades . The approval for the change was nearly unanimous , with only the Oklahoma City Thunder voting against the change and the Dallas Mavericks abstaining from voting .","entities":[],"facts":[]}
